  prayerLibrary: [
    { section: "Thanksgiving", text: "Father, we thank You. We thank You for life, for breath, for our families, our children, our provisions. We thank You for protecting us from every attack of the wicked. We thank You that we are still alive, still moving, still breathing, still seeing. Thank You Jesus, thank You Father. Blessed be Your name, O Lord. In the mighty name of Jesus. Amen." },
    { section: "Repentance", text: "Father, forgive me of every sin that I have committed. Every hidden sin, O Lord, let it be wiped off. Let it be washed. Any bitterness, any wrath, any anger, any evil speaking that will stand in the way of my testimony, in the way of my deliverance, that will hinder my prayers and my open heavens — Lord, wash it away from me tonight. Create in me a clean heart and renew a right spirit within me. In the mighty name of Jesus. Amen." },
    { section: "Forgiveness", text: "Lord, I forgive every person who has hurt me — knowingly and unknowingly. I release them. I let them go. Every bitterness, every wrath, every anger, every clamour, every evil speaking — I put it away from me now with all malice. I choose to be kind and tenderhearted, forgiving as God for Christ's sake has forgiven me. In Jesus' name. Amen." },
    { section: "Inviting the Holy Ghost", text: "Holy Spirit, we invite You into this atmosphere. Come, Holy Ghost. Baptize us with fire. Go ahead of us tonight. Destroy every barrier and every hindrance in our lives that would stop our deliverance. Reveal to us the covenants we do not know of, the covenants we have forgotten, the covenants entered on our behalf. Holy Spirit, hover over our lives, hover over our homes, hover over our families. In the mighty name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth. Amen." },
    { section: "Renunciation of covenants", text: "As I drink the blood of Jesus, I call upon the power of the Holy Ghost. I call upon the power in the blood of Jesus. I take back every ground I gave to Satan by any covenant knowingly or unknowingly in my life. In the name of Jesus, by the power of the Holy Ghost, by the blood of Jesus Christ, I break every covenant that is not ordained by God in my life, in my family's life, and in my children's lives. In Jesus' name. Amen." },
    { section: "Breaking ancestral covenants", text: "By the blood of Jesus, I renounce every ancestral covenant from my father's side and from my mother's side. Every covenant made by my great-grandparents, my grandparents, my parents — I disannul it now. Every idol my ancestors served, every altar they built, every animal they sacrificed, every blood they poured — I disconnect myself and my generations from every one of those covenants by the blood of Jesus. The chain is broken. In Jesus' name. Amen." },
    { section: "Breaking sexual covenants", text: "By the blood of Jesus, I renounce every covenant entered through sexual sin. Every word I spoke during sex — 'I will never leave you', 'I will be with you forever', 'I will have all my children with you' — I renounce every one of those words. Every ex-partner, every ex-husband, every ex-wife, every ex-boyfriend, every ex-girlfriend — I disconnect myself from every soul tie. Every demon released to enforce that covenant, I command you to leave now in the name of Jesus." },
    { section: "Breaking third-party altar covenants", text: "By the blood of Jesus, I renounce every covenant entered on my behalf. Every message I sent, every money I gave, every altar I did not visit but somebody visited for me — I disconnect from every one of those altars by the blood of Jesus. Every witch doctor who prayed for me, every native doctor, every so-called pastor who was not a pastor — I disconnect. In Jesus' name. Amen." },
    { section: "Breaking curses attached to covenants", text: "By the fire of the Holy Ghost, I break every curse of failure — break, break, break. Every curse of poverty — break, break, break. Every curse of family breakup — break, break, break. Every curse of depression — break, break, break. Every curse of bad reputation — break, break, break. Every curse of personal destruction or suicide — break, break, break. Every curse of chronic sickness — break, break, break. Every curse of unprofitable hard work — break, break, break. Every curse of evil dedication — break, break, break. In the name of Jesus. Amen." },
    { section: "Anointing with oil / declaring blessings", text: "As I anoint myself with this oil, I release myself from every bondage of evil ancestors in the mighty name of Jesus. Every demonic dedication over my life — cancel. Every evil authority of family idols — I break by the fire of the Holy Ghost. Every witchcraft in my family, every family spirit — I break in the name of Jesus. Every evil authority of remote control power — destroyed. Every evil authority of manipulation — destroyed. I anoint myself with this fire and I walk in freedom, favor, healing, and breakthrough. In Jesus' name. Amen." },
    { section: "Sealing", text: "Father, cover me with the blood as I go to bed tonight. Send Your angels to surround me. Let no evil come near my dwelling. Give me peaceful sleep in the name of Jesus. Let no weapon formed against me prosper. Every retaliation is cancelled, destroyed, and returned back to sender. I am covered by the blood. I shall testify of Your goodness from tonight. In the mighty name of Jesus. Amen." },
    { section: "Thanksgiving (closing)", text: "Father, we thank You for deliverance. We thank You for restoration. We thank You for healing. We thank You for protection. We thank You for victory. We give You thanks for every chain that is broken tonight. We give You thanks for every yoke that is destroyed. We give You thanks for every evil covenant that is cancelled by the blood of Jesus Christ. Let our testimonies manifest speedily. Let peace replace our fear, joy replace our sorrow, from tonight. In the mighty name of Jesus. Amen." },
    { section: "Salvation & Rededication", text: "Lord Jesus, I repent of my sins and surrender my life to Christ. Wash me clean. I believe that Jesus Christ is the Son of God, that He died on the cross for my sins, and rose again on the third day for my victory. I believe in my heart and make a confession with my mouth that Jesus is my Saviour and Lord. I receive eternal life in Jesus' name. Amen." }
  ],

